  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that CID 11603911 may be associated with LNCaP through multiple indirect pathways. The target of CID 11603911 is 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which is targeted by 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol, a compound that in turn targets LNCaP. Similarly, CID 11603911 is also associated with Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is targeted by Lethedioside B and Palmyramide A, both of which also target LNCaP. These findings indicate that CID 11603911 may exert its biological effects through different molecular mechanisms, potentially influencing LNCaP through various pathways. The evidence suggests a possible relationship between CID 11603911 and LNCaP, but the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
